		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD 9600]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4731&amp;p=35001#p35001"><![CDATA[
Make sure you are turning the radio off from the front panel button. That allows it to save the last settings to flash. Just removing the power externally does not do this and relies on the internal backup battery which can easily become discharged. <br><br>You may also need to leave the radio connected to a power supply for an extended time (several days) to recharge the internal backup battery. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Sun Jan 05, 2025 11:01 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
